-- ownership (v2; R-5.5.6): an alias chain through three modules to a
-- private function. `Lib.a1` names `Mid.a2`, which names `Mid`'s private
-- `priv`: `Main` cannot see `priv`, and `Lib` publishes no class for `a1`,
-- whose function is not its own; `Mid` publishes `priv`'s class as `a2`'s,
-- and the call applies it. `kept` reads `xs` after the call and is refused
-- `later-use`; `owned` reads nothing after and is accepted.
import Lib


pub kept : List Int → List Int × List Int
kept xs = ( Lib.a1 xs, xs )


pub owned : List Int → List Int
owned xs = Lib.a1 xs
